hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2751","**\nNarrated to us Yaḥyā ibn Ḥakīm, narrated to us Abū ʿĀṣim, from Ibn Jurayj, who informed me Sulaymān al-Aḥwal, that Ṭāwūs informed him that the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) passed by a man who was circumambulating the Kaʿbah while leading another man by a nose-ring. So the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) cut it off and then ordered him to lead him by his hand.\n\nHe (Ṭāwūs) said: The Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) also passed by a man who was circumambulating the Kaʿbah while leading another man by a strap or a thread or something similar. So the Prophet (ﷺ) cut it off and said, \Lead him by his hand.\"""""""
"2752","**\nNarrated to us Sulayman al-Aḥwal who said: All of them [the narrators] informed me that Ṭāwūs informed him that Ibn ʿAbbās (RA) said that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:\n*\Indeed"","" there is a concession in speaking during the Tawāf when there is a need.\""*\n\nAbū Bakr [al-Bukhārī] (RA) said: \""This narration indicates the allowance of speaking during the Tawāf when there is a need or necessity.\"""""""
